 r←GetReadmeUrls(projectUrl version);ver;group;repo;path;tag
⍝ Returns a two-column matrix with the URLs a package's README might be fetched from:
⍝ [;1] the "raw.githubusercontent.com" URL to fetch it from
⍝ [;2] the matching "github.com/.../blob/..." URL, recorded for attributing the source
⍝ One row per tag spelling worth trying, the most likely one first: Tatin release tags read
⍝ "v1.2.3", but tags older than that convention read "1.2.3".
⍝ The result is empty when `projectUrl` does not point at a GitHub repository: nothing else
⍝ is supported, and guessing would attach a stranger's README to a package.
⍝ Note that the tag decides: fetching from the default branch is deliberately not offered,
⍝ because that would document a release with instructions that may not work for it.
 r←0 2⍴''
 ver←version
 ver←(¯1+ver⍳'+')↑ver                               ⍝ Build metadata is no part of a tag
 path←projectUrl
 :If 0=≢ver
 :OrIf 0=≢path
     :Return
 :EndIf
 :If '/'=¯1↑path                                    ⍝ A trailing slash is common and harmless
     path←¯1↓path
 :EndIf
 :If '.git'≡⎕C ¯4↑path
     path←¯4↓path
 :EndIf
 :If 0=≢path←GetGitHubPath path
     :Return
 :EndIf
 (group repo)←path
 :For tag :In ('v',ver)ver
     r⍪←(GetRawGitHubUrl group repo tag'README.md')(GetBlobGitHubUrl group repo tag'README.md')
 :EndFor
